Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1D-GWPObject-LIST", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996335738629848*^9, 3.9963357454370737`*^9}, 
   3.996672469810019*^9, {3.996753015752389*^9, 3.996753019402701*^9}, 
   3.996753795862422*^9, {3.997473895005803*^9, 3.997473895666403*^9}, {
   3.9974763808748283`*^9, 
   3.9974763811434097`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6386a0ad-7da2-4e20-bb93-\
bccdee17a057"],

Cell["\<\
The 1D-GWPObject-LIST test suite validates the framework\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
numerical execution capabilities by ensuring that the GWP and GWPObject \
interfaces correctly process user-supplied lists of numerical values. \
Building upon the structural and routing verifications of the previous \
suites, this automated test is algorithmically generated directly from the \
object\[CloseCurlyQuote]s internal property dictionaries to guarantee \
comprehensive evaluation. It systematically proves that passing vectorized \
lists of numerical coordinates\[LongDash]across the temporal, spatial, \
energy, and cumulative domains\[LongDash]strictly yields the exact same \
arrays as mapping the underlying functions over those individual values. This \
confirms the framework\[CloseCurlyQuote]s mathematical stability and \
equivalence when performing batch numerical evaluations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.996758107379475*^9, {3.997473900016397*^9, 
   3.997473907303217*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8d92a564-a039-4460-bca0-\
fca6eabd1847"],

